  "body": "Follow-up of #1883 (PR for Waterjet Profile).\n\n## Problem\n\nThe Waterjet Profile operation stores its cut data as explicit numbers: cut feed, pierce time, abrasive delay and an optional kerf override. The nozzle tool can hold waterjet recipes (`CuttingRow.waterjet`, #1881). `camcraft_tools::cutting_rows::waterjet_row_for(rows, material, thickness)` finds a recipe. The operation does not read the recipe. The user must type the numbers from the recipe by hand.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe generation job (`crates/app/src/operation/job.rs`) does not carry the stock material. Many open PRs change `job.rs`, so #1883 did not change it.\n\n## Wanted\n\n- An option on the Waterjet Profile: \"use the nozzle's recipe\".\n- When it is on, the generator reads the recipe for the stock material and the sheet thickness (top minus bottom). The recipe gives the kerf, the cut feed, the pierce time and the abrasive delay.\n- No recipe for that material and thickness: refuse by name. Do not use the nearest thickness.\n- The UI page and the `.camproj` DTO show and keep the option. An absent key means \"off\", so older files load without a change.\n\n## Done means\n\nA test generates a Waterjet Profile from a recipe, and a test pins the refusal when no recipe matches.\n",
